                                        <PARAMETER-DATA-PROTOTYPE UUID="0e0b8c00-8f51-5814-18d6-a3798f495ccf">
                                            <SHORT-NAME>STCWkt_f_ClchCmdCapFactor</SHORT-NAME>
                                            <DESC>
                                                <L-2 L="FOR-ALL">###Description
Output table for scaling capabilities with clutch command in active range

###Usage
Use this table to calibrate how the P3/P4 motor capabilities shall be scaled as function of clutch pedal posistion

###Calibration Note
This is to be used for manual transmission and is only used depending on the calibration STCWke_e_CluToEmFactMethod







</L-2>
                                            </DESC>
                                            <CATEGORY>CURVE</CATEGORY>
                                            <SW-DATA-DEF-PROPS>
                                                <SW-DATA-DEF-PROPS-VARIANTS>
                                                    <SW-DATA-DEF-PROPS-CONDITIONAL>
                                                        <SW-CALIBRATION-ACCESS>READ-WRITE</SW-CALIBRATION-ACCESS>
                                                        <SW-IMPL-POLICY>STANDARD</SW-IMPL-POLICY>
                                                    </SW-DATA-DEF-PROPS-CONDITIONAL>
                                                </SW-DATA-DEF-PROPS-VARIANTS>
                                            </SW-DATA-DEF-PROPS>
                                            <TYPE-TREF DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">/STCW_pkg/STCW_dt/ApplDataTypes/Appl_STCWkt_f_ClchCmdCapFactor</TYPE-TREF>
                                            <INIT-VALUE>
                                                <CONSTANT-REFERENCE>
                                                    <SHORT-LABEL>STCWkt_f_ClchCmdCapFactor</SHORT-LABEL>
                                                    <CONSTANT-REF DEST="CONSTANT-SPECIFICATION">/STCW_pkg/STCW_dt/Ground/STCWkt_f_ClchCmdCapFactor</CONSTANT-REF>
                                                </CONSTANT-REFERENCE>
                                            </INIT-VALUE>
                                        </PARAMETER-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
                                        <PARAMETER-DATA-PROTOTYPE UUID="133ac98d-3542-5085-cf67-6ce51c3f58f3">
                                            <SHORT-NAME>STCWkt_r_MtrAMinLimScl</SHORT-NAME>
                                            <DESC>
                                                <L-2 L="FOR-ALL">###Description
This table scales tha available Min torque from the P1 motor

###Usage
Use this table to prevent the P1motor to start rotating backwards.

###Calibration Note
This is intended to be used if having a P1 motor
</L-2>
                                            </DESC>
                                            <CATEGORY>CURVE</CATEGORY>
                                            <SW-DATA-DEF-PROPS>
                                                <SW-DATA-DEF-PROPS-VARIANTS>
                                                    <SW-DATA-DEF-PROPS-CONDITIONAL>
                                                        <SW-CALIBRATION-ACCESS>READ-WRITE</SW-CALIBRATION-ACCESS>
                                                        <SW-IMPL-POLICY>STANDARD</SW-IMPL-POLICY>
                                                    </SW-DATA-DEF-PROPS-CONDITIONAL>
                                                </SW-DATA-DEF-PROPS-VARIANTS>
                                            </SW-DATA-DEF-PROPS>
                                            <TYPE-TREF DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">/STCW_pkg/STCW_dt/ApplDataTypes/Appl_STCWkt_r_MtrAMinLimScl</TYPE-TREF>
                                            <INIT-VALUE>
                                                <CONSTANT-REFERENCE>
                                                    <SHORT-LABEL>STCWkt_r_MtrAMinLimScl</SHORT-LABEL>
                                                    <CONSTANT-REF DEST="CONSTANT-SPECIFICATION">/STCW_pkg/STCW_dt/Ground/STCWkt_r_MtrAMinLimScl</CONSTANT-REF>
                                                </CONSTANT-REFERENCE>
                                            </INIT-VALUE>
                                        </PARAMETER-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
                                        <PARAMETER-DATA-PROTOTYPE UUID="436c735e-8b9a-590a-258f-f9fd6da749c6">
                                            <SHORT-NAME>STCWkt_r_PartOfTotalCpbyD</SHORT-NAME>
                                            <DESC>
                                                <L-2 L="FOR-ALL">###Description
Part of total torque, Drive-Rampout. Scales the torque capbility that can accelerate the vehicle in the opposite direction to the driver intended direction.

###Usage
Use this table to define how the torque capabilities shall be scaled when the speed is close to zero, i.e. approaching an unwanted direction.

###Calibration Note
</L-2>
                                            </DESC>
                                            <CATEGORY>CURVE</CATEGORY>
                                            <SW-DATA-DEF-PROPS>
                                                <SW-DATA-DEF-PROPS-VARIANTS>
                                                    <SW-DATA-DEF-PROPS-CONDITIONAL>
                                                        <SW-CALIBRATION-ACCESS>READ-WRITE</SW-CALIBRATION-ACCESS>
                                                        <SW-IMPL-POLICY>STANDARD</SW-IMPL-POLICY>
                                                    </SW-DATA-DEF-PROPS-CONDITIONAL>
                                                </SW-DATA-DEF-PROPS-VARIANTS>
